{
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Every file-based source the panel is meant to handle, side by side: GeoParquet through DuckDB, GeoJSON and CSV through Infinity. Each panel is deliberately unconfigured — no saved mapConfig — so what renders is what autodetection alone produces.",
  "editable": true,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Data sources\n\nEvery panel arrives at the same place — a kepler layer — by a different road. None of them has saved layers: what is drawn is what autodetection infers from the columns. The only thing fixed is the viewport, because without it the map starts too close and part of the dataset falls off screen.\n\n| Panel | Source | How the geometry arrives |\n|---|---|---|\n| GeoParquet · points | DuckDB `read_parquet` | `latitude` / `longitude` columns |\n| GeoParquet · zones | DuckDB + the `spatial` extension | `ST_AsGeoJSON(ST_GeomFromWKB(...))` |\n| GeoJSON · zones | Infinity, from a URL | a `geometry` object serialised to a string |\n| CSV · points | Infinity, from a URL | kepler's `<prefix>_latitude` convention |\n| CSV · zones | Infinity, from a URL | WKT in a `geometry` column |\n\nThe files come from `testdata/`, served by the `sources-data` container and mounted at `/testdata` inside Grafana."
      },
      "title": "",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
        "uid": "duckdb"
      },
      "description": "Plain columns, no spatial extension involved. The parquet carries point_latitude/point_longitude alongside the geometry, and aliasing them to latitude/longitude is what the plugin's own detectFields matches on.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "showSidePanel": true,
        "timeSync": "off",
        "mapConfig": {
          "version": "v1",
          "config": {
            "mapState": {
              "latitude": -2.905,
              "longitude": -79.0,
              "zoom": 11.5,
              "bearing": 0,
              "pitch": 0,
              "dragRotate": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "uid": "duckdb"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": 1,
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT\n  name,\n  category,\n  visitors,\n  point_latitude  AS latitude,\n  point_longitude AS longitude\nFROM read_parquet('/testdata/cuenca-points.parquet')",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "GeoParquet · points (DuckDB)",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
        "uid": "duckdb"
      },
      "description": "kepler reads no form of WKB, so the geometry has to become GeoJSON. Note there is no ST_GeomFromWKB call: DuckDB's spatial extension reads a GeoParquet geometry column as a native GEOMETRY (carrying its EPSG:4326 CRS), not as a BLOB. The CAST to VARCHAR is not decoration — ST_AsGeoJSON returns DuckDB's JSON type and the data source's Go driver cannot Scan that into a string.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "showSidePanel": true,
        "timeSync": "off",
        "mapConfig": {
          "version": "v1",
          "config": {
            "mapState": {
              "latitude": -2.905,
              "longitude": -79.0,
              "zoom": 11.5,
              "bearing": 0,
              "pitch": 0,
              "dragRotate": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
            "uid": "duckdb"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": 1,
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT\n  name,\n  population,\n  CAST(ST_AsGeoJSON(geometry) AS VARCHAR) AS geojson\nFROM read_parquet('/testdata/cuenca-zones.parquet')",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "GeoParquet · zones (DuckDB + spatial)",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
        "uid": "infinity"
      },
      "description": "A GeoJSON URL flattened by Infinity's backend parser. Typing the geometry column as String is what makes Infinity serialise the nested object to a GeoJSON string; the panel then autodetects the geojson column as geometry.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "showSidePanel": true,
        "timeSync": "off",
        "mapConfig": {
          "version": "v1",
          "config": {
            "mapState": {
              "latitude": -2.905,
              "longitude": -79.0,
              "zoom": 11.5,
              "bearing": 0,
              "pitch": 0,
              "dragRotate": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "columns": [
            {
              "selector": "properties.name",
              "text": "name",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "selector": "properties.population",
              "text": "population",
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "selector": "geometry",
              "text": "geojson",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ],
          "datasource": {
            "type": "yesoreyeram-infinity-datasource",
            "uid": "infinity"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "parser": "backend",
          "refId": "A",
          "root_selector": "features",
          "source": "url",
          "type": "json",
          "url": "http://sources-data/cuenca-zones.geojson",
          "url_options": {
            "method": "GET"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "GeoJSON · zones (Infinity, from a URL)",
      "type": "ubica-keplergl-panel"
    },
